# hsk py check

After completing code changes, run this cycle from the project root (with venv active):

1. `hsk py ruff-sort-docs`
2. `hsk py check`

There is no `hsk py ruff` command. Use `hsk py ruff-sort` only when docs generation is not needed; prefer `ruff-sort-docs` before `check`.

If `hsk` fails with `Access is denied` on `hsk.exe` (often because the app is running from the same venv), close the app or run the equivalent checks via `python -m` (`ruff`, `ty`, `pytest`) and still report that the full `hsk py check` could not complete.

Fix until `hsk py check` passes. Repeat this cycle up to **3 times maximum**. If it still fails after 3 iterations, stop and report the remaining errors.

Do not finish while `hsk py check` still fails, unless the failure is environmental and cannot be fixed in code.

## Cross-project check

Linked external projects:

- `harrix-pylib`
- `harrix-pyssg`

Run `hsk py ruff-sort-docs` and `hsk py check` in an external project **only if that project itself was modified** in this session. Do not check unmodified linked projects.

If an external project was modified: fix until `hsk py check` passes there (up to **3 times maximum**), unless the failure is environmental and cannot be fixed in code.
